# Signal — Cursor Workspace Rules

You are **Cursor**, collaborating in parallel with **Antigravity** on **Signal** (by **Signal Design, Inc.**), a cloud-native, AI-Agent-First EDA platform (Pure Rust core engine in Kubernetes + Node.js BFF + Angular 19+ web IDE).

## 1. Canonical Source of Truth & Phase Gate
- Treat `AGENTS.md` and `architecture/README.md` as the **single source of truth**. Read `AGENTS.md` in full before starting major work and consult the matching `architecture/01..12-*.md` spec for your task domain.
- **Phase Gate:** Check `AGENTS.md` Section 1 and `coordination/TASK_BOARD.md`. Do **not** write production application code while in Architecture & Planning phase unless the user explicitly initiates Phase 0.

## 2. Mandatory Session-Start Ritual
1. Run `git fetch origin --prune`.
2. Read `coordination/TASK_BOARD.md`, `coordination/agents/antigravity.md` (**read-only**), and any new files under `coordination/handoffs/`.
3. Confirm your planned `touched_paths` have **zero overlap** with any active Antigravity task.
4. Branch from `origin/main` using `cursor/<task-id>-<slug>` (or `contract/<task-id>-<slug>` for serialized contract-only PRs). Never push parallel feature work directly to `main`.

## 3. Deadlock-Free Rules for Cursor
- **Default Swimlane (Lane B):** `web/**` (Angular 19+ Standalone + Signals), `services/**` (Node.js 22 TypeScript BFF & Control Plane), and `ai/orchestrator/**` UI bridges—unless explicitly assigned a disjoint task on `TASK_BOARD.md`.
- **Contract-First (Zero Waiting):** If a new gRPC/OpenAPI/JSON contract is needed, land a small `contract/<task-id>-<slug>` PR on `main` FIRST so both IDEs rebase. Never wait/poll for Antigravity; build against frozen `contracts/` stubs.
- **Exclusive Journal:** Update ONLY `coordination/agents/cursor.md`. **NEVER edit `coordination/agents/antigravity.md`.** Write cross-IDE handoffs as new immutable files `coordination/handoffs/YYYYMMDD-<task-id>-cursor-to-ag.md`.
- **Migrations & Rebase:** Name DB migrations `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_cursor_<slug>.sql` (never sequential integers). Rebase onto `origin/main` before pushing/merging.

## 4. Non-Negotiable Product & Security Invariants
- **Rust owns physics & geometry (`ElectronicModule` trait):** Never implement SPICE, circuit math, DRC/LVS/PEX, routing, or Gerber/GDSII generation in Node.js or Angular.
- **Zero local design copies:** Never persist schematics, netlists, layouts, firmware, waveforms, or specs in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `IndexedDB`, Service Workers, or client downloads.
- **No export / no print / anti-screenshot:** Never add file download/export endpoints or print views for design artifacts. Preserve print-blocking, privacy curtains, watermarks, and Enterprise Zero-Leak pixel-stream mode.
- **Mandatory 2FA Authorized SFTP only:** Every SFTP server registration/edit/delete/release push (Enterprise AND Individual) MUST enforce fresh Step-Up 2FA (WebAuthn/TOTP), SSH host-key pinning, and immutable audit logging.
- **Local Mac Dev Mode:** Support Local Mac LLM (Ollama/MLX) as default and `Guest` @ `Signal Design, Inc.` ONLY behind strict compile-time (`dev-guest-auth`) + runtime (`SIGNAL_ENV=local` + loopback) guards that can never ship in production.
